WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.570
ROGER MARTINEZ:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.860
about VMware Engine, Apache
Cassandra, and Google Cloud

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.040
Next.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.060
I'm Roger Martinez.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.970
And welcome to "This
Week in Cloud,"

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.660
where we serve you
the lowest latency

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.730
news from the safety of home.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.400
For the past year, we've been
working to support customers

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.530
with VMware workloads.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.350
And now, we're happy to announce
that the effort has grown

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.840
into a fully managed service.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.200
Google Cloud VMware Engine
offers end-to-end support

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.140
to migrate and run your VMware
environments on Google Cloud

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.400
Platform.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.240
Check out the blog
to learn more.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.090
Apache Cassandra is an
open source database

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.400
built on a scale-out
architecture

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.910
to support applications with
a massive amount of data.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.000
To make it easier for customers
to deploy, manage, and scale

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.780
their Cassandra workloads, we're
introducing DataStax Astra,

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.990
with Cassandra as a service.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.280
Try it today and create
a Cassandra cluster

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.620
on Google Cloud in
minutes without worrying

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.240
about operational overhead.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.310
Google Cloud is dedicated
to helping customers

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.680
maximize their business
value without maximizing

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.269
their budget.

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:06.890
We offer many tools
to help developers

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.700
stay on top of their costs.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.850
But there are always
techniques and tips

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.730
that could help you
optimize your costs.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.160
This blog post covers
several high-level principles

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.710
that organizations can follow
to ensure that they're getting

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.615
the most out of their cloud.

00:01:21.615 --> 00:01:23.240
We've spent the last
few months working

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.090
to evolve Next 2020 into a
worthwhile digital experience.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.540
And now, we're pretty
proud of what we've built.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.610
Starting on July 14, join us
for a nine-week digital event.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.790
Next OnAir will offer
fresh content each week,

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.370
with over 200
sessions in total, all

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.710
built around providing
compelling content,

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.470
connecting you with experts,
and growing your skills.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.470
If you want to read more
about the announcements

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.890
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.020
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.090
Leave us a comment, or tweet us.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.530
We'll see you in the cloud.

